+# Viewfinder Spec - frame guides and focus peaking
+
+Status: APPROVED FOR IMPLEMENTATION (2026-08-25). Author: main session.
+Repository: `E:\coding3\ReC_sandbox\CRYENGINE_Source`, branch `dev`.
+
+## What it is
+
+Operator aids drawn over the final frame, the way a camera's viewfinder or a monitor does:
+- **Frame guides**: rule-of-thirds lines, centre cross, action/title safe areas, and an
+  aspect-ratio framing guide (lines or a translucent shade for a target aspect such as 2.39:1
+  while the viewport is 16:9 - different from the letterbox, which is part of the picture).
+- **Focus peaking**: edges that are inside the depth of field are tinted, so the operator sees
+  what is sharp without judging blur on a small monitor.
+
+Both are OVERLAYS: they are never part of the picture, they are editor-live so framing can
+be judged while authoring, and they must be trivially switchable off for recording.
+Everything lives in the PostAA composite (`PostAA.cfx` `PostAAComposites_PS`, after the
+letterbox mask - the last thing before grain/output), driven by cvars the component pushes.
+
+Build with the bundled CMake (targets `CryRenderD3D11` then `CinematicCamera`, Profile,
+sequential). Zero errors; zero warnings from our files. Do NOT deploy or commit. English only.
+
+---
+
+## A. Cvars (`Common/RendererCVars.h/.cpp`), registered next to `r_LensLetterbox`
+
+| cvar | type | default | meaning |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `r_LensGuides` | int (bitmask) | 0 | 1 = rule of thirds, 2 = centre cross, 4 = action safe (90%) + title safe (80%) rectangles, 8 = aspect framing guide. 0 = off. |
+| `r_LensGuideAspect` | float | 2.39 | Target aspect for the framing guide (bit 8): the band of that aspect centred in the viewport is outlined and the outside is shaded. |
+| `r_LensGuideOpacity` | float | 0.6 | Line opacity, 0..1. |
+| `r_LensPeaking` | float | 0 | Focus peaking strength, 0 = off. Edge response inside the depth of field is tinted with this weight. |
+| `r_LensPeakingNear` | float | 0 | Near limit of the in-focus band, metres (pushed by the component from its thin-lens DOF bounds). |
+| `r_LensPeakingFar` | float | 0 | Far limit, metres. |
+| `r_LensPeakingColor` | int | 1 | 1 = red, 2 = green, 3 = blue, 4 = yellow, 5 = white. |
+| `r_LensOverlays` | int | 1 | Master switch for ALL viewfinder overlays (guides + peaking). 0 kills them regardless of the other cvars - the recording switch. |
+
+Help texts: one sentence each, mention "viewfinder overlay, never part of the picture".
+
+## B. Renderer (`GraphicsPipeline/PostAA.cpp`, `PostAA.cfx`)
+
+`PostAA.cpp` (the block that sets `vLensDistortionParams`): add two more PS constants
+- `vLensGuideParams` = (guides bitmask as float, guideAspect, guideOpacity, viewport aspect)
+- `vLensPeakingParams` = (peaking strength, near, far, colour index as float)
+with `r_LensOverlays == 0` forcing the bitmask and the strength to 0. Bind the LINEAR depth
+texture (`m_graphicsPipelineResources.m_pTexLinearDepth`, PointClamp) to a free PS slot of the
+composition pass when peaking is on (binding it always is acceptable if simpler; say which).
+
+`PostAA.cfx`, `PostAAComposites_PS`, inserted AFTER the letterbox mask block and BEFORE the
+`%_RT_SAMPLE2` sharpening (so guides are never sharpened) - actually place it after
+`ApplyFilmGrain` and the `saturate` so overlays are clean of grain and sharpening; keep them
+before the `%_RT_SAMPLE4` range compression:
+
+```
+// --- Viewfinder overlays: not part of the picture. ---
+// Focus peaking: luminance edge (4-tap Sobel-ish on the ALREADY FINAL colour) x in-focus
+// weight from linear depth. The in-focus weight is 1 inside [near, far] with a soft
+// 5% falloff on either side; edge strength is the max abs difference to the 4 neighbours
+// scaled by 6 and saturated. Tint = lerp(colour, peakColour, edge * inFocus * strength).
+// Guides: 1px lines (use fwidth-free pixel test: abs(coord - target) < 0.5 texel) blended
+// with guideOpacity: thirds at 1/3, 2/3 both axes; centre cross 6% of height long;
+// action safe = centred 90% rectangle, title safe = 80%; aspect guide = band of
+// guideAspect (height fraction = viewportAspect / guideAspect when guideAspect wider,
+// width fraction = guideAspect / viewportAspect when narrower) outlined, outside shaded
+// by multiplying the colour with (1 - 0.5 * guideOpacity).
+```
+Peaking depth: `depth = texDepth.Load(...).x * PS_NearFarClipDist.y` (linear metres), sampled
+at the SAME remapped coordinate `tcFinal` the picture used (squeeze / distortion), or the
+overlay would sit on the unremapped frame. Guides are drawn in viewport space (they are
+monitor markings, not picture content), so they use `IN.baseTC`, NOT `tcFinal`.
+
+## C. Component (`CinematicCameraComponent.h/.cpp`)
+
+New property group `SCineViewfinderParams` ('gvfd', label "Viewfinder"), placed LAST in the
+group order (after Anamorphic):
+
+| member | tag | label | type | default | description |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `bShowGuides` | 'vgon' | Frame Guides | bool | false | Draw the selected framing guides over the frame. Viewfinder overlay, never part of the picture. |
+| `bThirds` | 'vthd' | Rule Of Thirds | bool | true | |
+| `bCentre` | 'vctr' | Centre Cross | bool | true | |
+| `bSafeAreas` | 'vsaf' | Safe Areas | bool | false | Action safe (90%) and title safe (80%). |
+| `bAspectGuide` | 'vasp' | Aspect Guide | bool | false | Outline the target aspect band and shade the outside. |
+| `guideAspect` | 'vgas' | Guide Aspect | Range<1,4,1,3> | 2.39 | Target aspect of the framing guide (2.39, 1.85, 1.33 ...). |
+| `guideOpacity` | 'vgop' | Guide Opacity | Range<0,1,0,1> | 0.6 | |
+| `peaking` | 'vpk_' | Focus Peaking | Range<0,2,0,1> | 0.0 | Tint in-focus edges. 0 = off. Uses this camera's thin-lens depth of field as the in-focus band. |
+| `peakingColour` | 'vpkc' | Peaking Colour | Range<1,5,1,5,int> | 1 | 1 red, 2 green, 3 blue, 4 yellow, 5 white. |
+| `bOverlaysInGame` | 'vgam' | Overlays In Game Mode | bool | false | Keep the overlays on in game / simulation mode. Off = editor only, so a recording never contains them. |
+
+`ApplyViewfinder()` / `RestoreViewfinder()` with the usual latch: pushes `r_LensGuides`
+(bitmask from the four bools, 0 when `bShowGuides` is off), `r_LensGuideAspect`,
+`r_LensGuideOpacity`, `r_LensPeaking`, `r_LensPeakingNear/Far` (from `ComputeDOFBounds()`),
+`r_LensPeakingColor`, and `r_LensOverlays` = (editing || bOverlaysInGame) ? 1 : 0 where
+"editing" is `gEnv->IsEditing()`. Gate with `CanDriveRenderState()`. It is EDITOR-LIVE like
+lens character: call it from the same places `ApplyLensCharacter()` is called (UPDATE,
+PROPERTY_CHANGED, FinalizeGameCamera) and restore it in `RestoreLensCharacter`'s company:
+add `RestoreViewfinder()` to `RestoreAllEffects()` and its latch to `ClearSavedBaselines()`.
+Peaking near/far must be re-pushed every frame (focus pulls move them).
+
+## D. Docs (English)
